---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <main>

    <!-- Header -->
    <section class="pt-40 pb-16 lg:pt-48 lg:pb-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 font-medium uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-black leading-[1.1] tracking-tight mb-6" style="text-wrap: balance;">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          How we collect, use, and protect your information.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Content -->
    <section class="pb-24 lg:pb-32">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none prose-headings:font-bold prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-h2:text-xl prose-h2:mt-14 prose-h2:mb-4 prose-h3:text-base prose-h3:mt-8 prose-h3:mb-3 prose-p:text-gray-500 prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-li:text-gray-500 prose-strong:text-black prose-a:text-black prose-a:underline prose-a:decoration-gray-300 hover:prose-a:decoration-black">

          <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>
            We collect information that you voluntarily provide to us through various forms on our website. We may share this information with our trusted partners who help us process information or provide services on our behalf. These partners are contractually required to handle your information securely and in compliance with applicable laws.
          </p>
          <p>Information we collect may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Assistance Request Forms:</strong> Personal information (name, contact details), address, and details about your assistance needs</li>
            <li><strong>Volunteer Applications:</strong> Contact information, availability, and relevant experience</li>
            <li><strong>Bug Reports:</strong> Email address (optional), page URL, and issue description</li>
            <li><strong>Donation Information:</strong> Contact details for donation receipts and acknowledgments</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To opt out of sharing your information with trusted partners, please contact us at <a href="mailto:compliance@donork.it">compliance@donork.it</a>.
          </p>

          <h3>Data Retention</h3>
          <p>
            We retain data for up to 360 days to ensure adequate time for program coordination, volunteer activities, or responding to assistance requests. Data is securely deleted afterward unless otherwise required by law. You may request deletion at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:compliance@donork.it">compliance@donork.it</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>Cookies &amp; Tracking Technologies</h2>
          <p>
            We and our third-party service providers use cookies and other tracking mechanisms to track information about your use of our website. We may combine this information with other personal information we collect from you.
          </p>
          <p>
            We currently do not respond to Do-Not-Track (DNT) browser settings. However, you can disable cookies or tracking technologies through your browser settings.
          </p>

          <h3>Session Cookies</h3>
          <p>
            Session cookies exist only during an online session and disappear when you close your browser. We use session cookies to uniquely identify you while logged in, process transactions, and verify your identity.
          </p>

          <h3>Persistent Cookies</h3>
          <p>
            Persistent cookies remain on your computer after you close your browser. We may use persistent cookies to track aggregate and statistical information about user activity.
          </p>

          <h3>Third-Party Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            We may use automated devices and applications to evaluate usage of our website. We do not share your personal information with these third parties. For details on the specific analytics services we use, see the "Third-Party Service Providers" section below.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-Party Service Providers</h2>
          <p>
            We use the following third-party service providers to operate our website and deliver our services. Each provider may receive certain personal information as described below. We encourage you to review their respective privacy policies.
          </p>

          <h3>Form Processing</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong><a href="https://formspree.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree</a></strong> &mdash; Processes submissions from our assistance request, volunteer application, and bug report forms. Receives name, email, phone number, address, and any other information you enter into those forms. <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree Privacy Policy</a></li>
            <li><strong><a href="https://townhall.gg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Townhall</a></strong> &mdash; Provides our backend data infrastructure for site variables such as impact statistics and needed items. Does not directly receive personal user data from form submissions. <a href="https://townhall.gg/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Townhall Privacy Policy</a></li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Payment Processing</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong><a href="https://stripe.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe</a></strong> &mdash; Processes all donation payments. When you make a donation, your email address and payment details are transmitted to Stripe to create a secure checkout session. Shelter in a Storm does not store your credit card information. <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe Privacy Policy</a></li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong><a href="https://analytics.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics</a></strong> &mdash; Collects anonymized usage data (pages visited, session duration, device type) to help us understand how visitors use our site. You can opt out via the <a href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/181881" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Maps &amp; Location</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong><a href="https://maps.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Maps</a></strong> &mdash; Embeds an interactive map on our food pantry page to help you find our location. Google may collect usage data when you interact with the embedded map. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Fonts &amp; Assets</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong><a href="https://fonts.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Fonts</a></strong> &mdash; Serves web fonts used on our site. When you load a page, your browser connects to Google's servers to download font files. <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Fonts Privacy</a></li>
            <li><strong><a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">jsDelivr</a></strong> &mdash; Serves the OpenDyslexic font file used by our accessibility settings. <a href="https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">jsDelivr Privacy Policy</a></li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            If you have questions about any of these providers or wish to opt out of data sharing, please contact us at <a href="mailto:compliance@donork.it">compliance@donork.it</a>.
          </p>

          <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Process and respond to your assistance requests</li>
            <li>Coordinate volunteer activities</li>
            <li>Improve our website and services</li>
            <li>Send you important updates about our services</li>
            <li>Process and acknowledge donations</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Security of Your Information</h2>
          <p>
            We employ encryption, secure servers, and access controls to protect your information. While no method of data transmission is 100% secure, we strive to use commercially acceptable means to safeguard your data.
          </p>

          <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our website is not intended for persons under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect information from persons under 13. If you believe we have inadvertently collected such information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:compliance@donork.it">compliance@donork.it</a> so we can promptly delete it.
          </p>

          <h2>Disclosure to Law Enforcement</h2>
          <p>
            We do not share your information with law enforcement agencies unless we are legally required to do so via a valid court order, subpoena, or warrant. Whenever possible, we will notify you of such requests unless legally prohibited from doing so.
          </p>

          <h2>Updates to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in our practices or legal requirements. Any updates will be posted on this page with the revised date.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or would like to request deletion of your information, please contact us at <a href="mailto:compliance@donork.it">compliance@donork.it</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-14 pt-6 border-t border-gray-100">
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-300">
            Last updated {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
